From 547fbace942d348e9ca902016a20321e54538311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 20:38:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] bluestore: initialize tracer + add read-path entry span

The bluestore-local-tracer change (PATCH 09/10 of the OTLP series)
introduced tracing::bluestore::tracer as a separate global to make
the os library self-contained (so ceph-bluestore-tool can link
without OSD symbols), and redirected the two existing call sites
in BlueStore.cc (queue_transactions, txc_aio_wait) from
tracing::osd::tracer to the new tracer. That fixed the link error
but never wired an exporter to the bluestore tracer, so those spans
silently dropped. nm shows the symbol in /usr/bin/ceph-osd but its
internal OTLP provider was null.

Initialize the bluestore tracer in OSD::init() alongside the osd
tracer so it gets its own OTLP exporter and TracerProvider with
service.name=bluestore.

Also add a 'bluestore_read' span at the entry of BlueStore::read
for GET-path observability. Orphan trace until librados gains an
IoCtx::operate read-overload accepting jspan_context (so RGW can
pass trace context to reads, mirroring writes); the span still
emits Prometheus latency histograms per OSD and is searchable in
Tempo. offset/length/op_flags as span attributes for TraceQL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc | 6 ++++++
 src/osd/OSD.cc                | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc b/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc
index 57ef882..e6ce1de 100644
--- a/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc
+++ b/src/os/bluestore/BlueStore.cc
@@ -12454,6 +12454,12 @@ int BlueStore::read(
   bufferlist& bl,
   uint32_t op_flags)
 {
+  auto read_span = tracing::bluestore::tracer.start_trace("bluestore_read");
+  if (read_span->IsRecording()) {
+    read_span->SetAttribute("offset", (int64_t)offset);
+    read_span->SetAttribute("length", (int64_t)length);
+    read_span->SetAttribute("op_flags", (int64_t)op_flags);
+  }
   auto start = mono_clock::now();
   Collection *c = static_cast<Collection *>(c_.get());
   const coll_t &cid = c->get_cid();
diff --git a/src/osd/OSD.cc b/src/osd/OSD.cc
index 8aa4dcb..074cb62 100644
--- a/src/osd/OSD.cc
+++ b/src/osd/OSD.cc
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@
 #include "common/numa.h"
 
 #include "os/ObjectStore.h"
+#include "os/bluestore/bluestore_tracer.h"
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBFUSE
 #include "os/FuseStore.h"
 #endif
@@ -3745,6 +3746,7 @@ int OSD::init()
   if (is_stopping())
     return 0;
   tracing::osd::tracer.init(cct, "osd", std::to_string(whoami));
+  tracing::bluestore::tracer.init(cct, "bluestore", std::to_string(whoami));
   tick_timer.init();
   tick_timer_without_osd_lock.init();
   service.recovery_request_timer.init();
